    "created_at": "2024-12-16T18:41:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-16T18:41:26Z",
    "body": "@scottaohara @zcorpan I thought the Invoker API would automatically add Aria attributes to the Accessibility API. That is what I would expect here. I agree that if it does not, then this would indeed require additional work via JS, etc.\r\n\r\nForgive me, but I thought one of the main reasons for the Invoker API is to reduce the need to add custom JS and to help with DX.\r\n\r\nWith that said is there any way now or future plans to toggle a class for any element without the need of JS. If not, then I think there should be. Even if it does not add accessibility and allow the Developer to work on that as another phase. I understand that accessibility should be high priority, but shouldn't that be on the developer and not a restriction on DX?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
